cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "anchorkey: zero-trust provenance for observed-entity telemetry under identifier drift"
abstract: >-
  A small, dependency-free framework for earning a stable identity for IoT and
  observed-entity telemetry: deterministic natural-key normalization under identifier
  drift, with (forthcoming) conservative entity matching and tamper-evident sealing. The
  reference implementation for a technical paper series on surrogate-key failure under
  identifier drift.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saha
    given-names: Rahul
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8172-0676"
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - IoT
  - telemetry
  - identity resolution
  - entity resolution
  - data quality
  - natural key
repository-code: "https://github.com/saharah-99/anchorkey"
